# Claim Jumper, a 3/3 with vigilance: "When this creature enters, if an opponent controls more lands than you, you may search
# your library for a Plains card and put it onto the battlefield tapped." (CR 603.4, 701.23). Bot1 plays no land and casts it
# on turn 3 with three Moxen, after Bot2 played an Island on turn 2: one land to none. A "Plains card" is any land with the
# subtype Plains, so a Plateau (a Mountain Plains) is one, while an Island and a Lightning Bolt are not (the refusals). Bot1
# takes the Plateau, which enters tapped, and then the lands are level (one each), so the process is not repeated. The
# library is shuffled once because it was searched.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Claim Jumper
Plains x4
Plateau
Island
Lightning Bolt
Plains x6

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Claim Jumper.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Claim Jumper.Keywords = Vigilance
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Accept
! Bot1.Search(Island)
! Bot1.Search(Lightning Bolt)
Bot1.Search(Plateau)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Plateau.Tapped = true
? Bot1.Shuffles = 1

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Ruby; Mox Pearl; Mox Emerald; Claim Jumper; Plateau
Bot1.Shuffles = 1
Bot2.Battlefield = Island
